# Slice 334 (Codex review of 333, item 1; the book, composition of the structural parts): merge composes the
# corresponding Structure parts of any operands by the same rules and the one map -- here two ordinary Structures with
# a nested part P, the second giving P a new field v: R's P holds u (from A) and v (from B), R's x is A's. A and B stay
# as written.
# Plan M11 5v: A and B live in the data part of main, R stays a root place; main reads the field counts of A and B.
sub: main () (
    A:
        int: x 1
        P(int: u 2)
    B:
        P(int: v 3)
    int: a_count 0
    int: a_p_count 0
    int: b_count 0
    int: b_p_count 0
)
    a_count := length(A)
    a_p_count := length(A\P)
    b_count := length(B)
    b_p_count := length(B\P)
@: R merge(main\data\A; main\data\B)
main()
int: u R\P\u
int: v R\P\v
int: x R\x
int: a_count main\data\a_count
int: a_p_count main\data\a_p_count
int: b_count main\data\b_count
int: b_p_count main\data\b_p_count
